{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And they returned and lodged a report against it.</b> And when they returned from scouting the land they roused the entire assembly against it by bringing forth an evil report — those men <b>died</b>. Every הוֹצָאַת דִּבָּה means training words — that one trains one's tongue against a person to speak about him, like ״דּוֹבֵב שִׂפְתֵי יְשֵׁנִים״ (Song of Songs 7). And there is such a thing for good and there is such a thing for evil — therefore it says here <b>bringers of an evil report of the land</b>, for there is a דִּבָּה that is good." "<b>A report.</b> פרליר״ש בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French parloir, 'to speak'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:56.730199257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}